345	2	20	400	simulacion	Resuelve la ecuación cuadrática $2x^{2}-5x-3=0$.	["$x = 3 \\\\text{ o } x = -\\\\frac{1}{2}$", "$x = -3 \\\\text{ o } x = \\\\frac{1}{2}$", "$x = \\\\frac{5}{2} \\\\text{ o } x = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$", "$x = 1 \\\\text{ o } x = -\\\\frac{3}{2}$"]	$x = 3 \\text{ o } x = -\\frac{1}{2}$	1) Calcula el discriminante: $D = (-5)^2-4\\cdot2\\cdot(-3)=49$. 2) Aplica la fórmula: $x = \\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{D}}{2a}=\\frac{5\\pm7}{4}$. 3) Obtienes $x=3$ y $x=-\\frac12$.	approved	800	10	2026-09-18 04:46:26.631904	practica
