349	2	20	800	simulacion	Resuelve la ecuación cuadrática $2x^{2}-5x-3=0$.	["$x=3 \\\\text{ o } x=-\\\\frac{1}{2}$", "$x=-3 \\\\text{ o } x=\\\\frac{1}{2}$", "$x=\\\\frac{5}{2} \\\\text{ o } x=-\\\\frac{3}{2}$", "$x=\\\\frac{7}{4} \\\\text{ o } x=-\\\\frac{1}{4}$"]	$x=3 \\text{ o } x=-\\frac{1}{2}$	1) Calcula el discriminante: $D=(-5)^{2}-4\\cdot2\\cdot(-3)=49$, $\\sqrt D=7$. 2) Aplica la fórmula: $x=\\frac{5\\pm7}{2\\cdot2}=\\frac{5\\pm7}{4}$. 3) Obtienes $x=3$ y $x=-\\frac12$.	approved	800	10	2026-09-18 04:47:18.459427	practica
